From 221485b914dbce50a95d78e807283b5288866a95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 06:04:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 66/75] perf(dsl): decode common ACIR opcodes straight from
 msgpack-compact bytes

The streaming program decoder unpacked every opcode into a msgpack object
tree and converted that into Acir:: structs. AssertZero, RANGE, MemoryOp and
BrilligCall (about 98% of the opcodes of the pinned flows) are now read
directly from the bytes: AssertZero into a reused Acir::Opcode::AssertZero
whose coefficient buffers are recycled between opcodes, RANGE and MemoryOp
into their Acir:: values, and BrilligCall only for the witness indices that
update the maximum witness index. Any other opcode or unexpected layout falls
back to the generic decoder. The conversion into AcirFormat is unchanged.

ChonkLoad: ~100 -> ~45 ms on transfer_1_recursions+private_fpc.
